Cookies, Local Storage (localStorage), and SessionStorage (sessionstorage) are all browser storage mechanisms used to store data on a web page.

1. **SessionStorage**: This is an object that stores data for one session only - typically when you navigate away from your current webpage without saving changes. It has no expiration date set at creation time but can be cleared using `window.sessionStorage.clear()` method if needed.

```javascript
